{"type":"after","callId":"call@512","endTime":55195.577,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/Headset, link and what survives\n    \n\nHeadset, link and what survives\nWhich state lives where — and what a BLE drop, a headset switch-off, or a power-cycle each wipe\n✅bench🔍app👥communityLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\nState survival matrix\n\n\nState\nBLE drop / reconnect\nHeadset switched off\nPower-cycle\nConf\n\n\n\nGame config (////)\n— (unknown) — re-send the full head after a reconnect\nGun sends  and drops the link; config: — (unknown)\nWiped —  then echoes  + \n✅bench\n\n\nAlive/dead + pools\nSurvives (a dead gun stays dead)\n—\nReset\n✅bench\n\n\nAmmo\nSurvives\n—\nWiped\n✅bench\n\n\n team / LED colour\nSurvives; colour is painted at \n—\nReset\n✅bench\n\n\n\nPersists\nPersists\nPersists (only the official app rewrites it)\n✅bench\n\n\nPlayer id ( t1)\nSurvives with config\n—\nWiped (the USB  is separate and persistent)\n✅bench\n\n\nScore, clock, respawn timer\nNever on the gun\n—\n—\n✅bench\n\n\n fn-23 state ( token 2 at 0)\nPersists until \n—\nCleared\n✅bench\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7r (E1), §7n; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-24 $NAME; EMP recovery matrix)\nDEV-09diagram pendingThe matrix above as a grid graphic.Source: as above\nHeadset off = no BLE.Switching a linked headset off makes the gun send  and drop. A headset-less gun \"connects\", answers a quick , then dies within seconds and echoes nothing to a config head. A power-cycled gun needs its headset re-linked before BLE holds. A held link plus  echoes is the headset check — there is no dedicated probe. The official app silently drops a headset-less gun within ~1.2 s.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7m, §7r\nHeadset behaviours (native, autonomous — they work under any host's game head)\n\n\nHeadset LED\nWhen\nConf\n\n\n\nSlow rainbow blink\nDisconnected / not paired — the pre-game tell for \"this gun will not join\"\n✅bench (operator, repeatable)\n\n\nTeam colour (red/blue…)\nPre-game only; goes dark once the game starts\n✅bench (operator)\n\n\nDark\nDuring play — normal\n✅bench (operator)\n\n\nSource: docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-27 headset LED)\nOther headset facts\n\n\nFact\nSource\nConf\n\n\n\nThe headset syncs team colour from the tagger\nbench observation\n✅bench\n\n\n token 2 = headset firmware (); USB  shows headset version and battery\ncaptures / USB\n✅bench\n\n\nHeadset disconnecting mid-game locks the gun until it reconnects (anti-cheat); a gun booted with no headset shoots normally in local play\nBattle Company manual V7\n👥community\n\n\nHeadset pairing can take up to 3 minutes with many BT devices nearby\nmanual V7\n👥community\n\n\nHeadset sensor ids:  tok1 0 = front dome, 1 = back dome (4 = gun body)\nshield-isolated bench\n✅bench\n\n\nGun↔headset pairing PIN = the headset's serial, set via USB \nLaserTagMods note + USB\n✅bench 👥community\n\n\nHeadset LED commands //// exist; only  and  have been seen in use\nAPK + captures\n🔍app ✅bench\n\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7h, §7m, §7r, tok1 section; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-27)\nScreamers.A tagger left powered all day can stop holding BLE — advertising normally but connect-then-drop or hanging on connect — the community-documented \"screamer\" state. Power-rest guns between sessions; keep them charged (firmware won't re-pair below a battery threshold).Source: docs/gotchas.md; docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-26 screamer)\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@512"}
